37"],"issn_org":["0028646X"],"issue":"5","journal":"New Phytologist","pages":"1495-1504","status":"p","title":"New Phytologist","volume":"237"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85143884187"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-195909fa-b1e5-4ed2-adfb-69610843a5a8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A research agenda for nonvascular photoautotrophs under climate change","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-408586","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"In seagrass sediments, lucinid bivalves and their chemoautotrophic bacterial symbionts consume H2S, relying indirectly on the plant productivity for the presence of the reduced chemical. Additionally, the role of lucinid bivalves in N provisioning to the plant (through N-2 fixation by the symbionts) was hypothesized. Thus, lucinids may contribute to sediment detoxification and plant fitness. Seagrasses are subject to ever-increasing human pressure in coastal environments. Here, disentangling nested interactions between chemosynthetic lucinid bivalves and seagrass exposed to pollution may help to understand seagrass ecosystem dynamics and to develop successful seagrass restoration programs that consider the roles of animal-microbe symbioses. We evaluated the capacity of lucinid bivalves (Loripes orbiculatus) to promote nutrient cycling and seagrass (Cymodocea nodosa) growth during a 6-week mesocosm experiment. A fully crossed design was used to test for the effect of sediment contamination (metals, nutrients, and hydrocarbons) on plant and bivalve (alone or interacting) fitness, assessed by mortality, growth, and photosynthetic efficiency, and for the effect of their nested interaction on sediment biogeochemistry. Plants performed better in the contaminated sediment, where a larger pool of dissolved nitrogen combined with the presence of other trace elements allowed for an improved photosynthetic efficiency. In fact, pore water nitrogen accumulated during the experiment in the controls, while it was consumed in the contaminated sediment. This trend was accentuated when lucinids were present. Concurrently, the interaction between clams and plants benefitted both organisms and promoted plant growth irrespective of the sediment type. In particular, the interaction with lucinid clams resulted in higher aboveground biomass of C. nodosa in terms of leaf growth, leaf surface, and leaf biomass. Our results consolidate the notion that nested interactions involving animal-microbe associations promote ecosystem functioning, and potentially help designing unconventional seagrass restoration strategies that exploit chemosynthetic symbioses.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Cardini, Ulisse","Marin-Guirao, Lazaro","Montilla, Luis M.","Marzocchi, Ugo","Chiavarini, Salvatore","Rimauro, Juri","Quero, Grazia Marina","Petersen, Jillian M.","Procaccini, Gabriele"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-227486"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Italy","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Spanish Institute of Oceanography","Stazione Zoologica Anton Dohrn Napoli","University of Vienna"],"keyword":["Cymodocea nodosa","Ecosystem restoration","GROWTH","MARINE","Nature based solutions","Nitrogen fixation","Posidonia oceanica","Restoration","meadows"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nested interactions between chemosynthetic lucinid bivalves and seagrass promote ecosystem functioning in contaminated sediments","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2022.918675","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-227486","identifier":[{"id":"35937361","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000837122300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85135447259","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9355091","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-ac238613-38df-41f2-9eee-fe04a904468c"],"keyword":["Bagnoli-Coroglio","Cymodocea nodosa","GROWTH","Loripes orbiculatus","MARINE","MEADOWS","MEDITERRANEAN SEAGRASSES","NITROGEN-FIXATION","POSIDONIA-OCEANICA","RESTORATION","chemosynthetic symbioses","ecological facilitation","ecosystem restoration","nature-based solutions","sediment contamination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2EABAAA7FC16FAED732B395CA7E8AF13"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpls.2022.918675","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"stazione zoologica anton dohrn napoli","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Stazione Zoologica Anton Dohrn Napoli","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"spanish institute of oceanography","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Spanish Institute of Oceanography","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Biology, Department of Biology - Microbiology","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, WATEC, Centre for Water Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"at","key":"university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Vienna","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulisse","key":"cardinipau","last":"Cardini","name":"Cardini, Ulisse","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lazaro","key":"maringuiraopau","last":"Marin-Guirao","name":"Marin-Guirao, Lazaro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis M.","key":"montillapau","last":"Montilla","name":"Montilla, Luis M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ugo","key":"marzocchipau","last":"Marzocchi","locid":"29341b14-1004-489c-9d94-978bbdb9a01b","name":"Marzocchi, Ugo","orcid":"0000-0002-4746-9944","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Salvatore","key":"chiavarinipau","last":"Chiavarini","name":"Chiavarini, Salvatore","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Juri","key":"rimauropau","last":"Rimauro","name":"Rimauro, Juri","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Grazia Marina","key":"queropau","last":"Quero","name":"Quero, Grazia Marina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jillian M.","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Jillian M.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gabriele","key":"procaccinipau","last":"Procaccini","name":"Procaccini, Gabriele","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35937361"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fpls.2022.918675","issn":["1664462X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Plant Science","paperid":"918675","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Plant Science","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135447259"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ac238613-38df-41f2-9eee-fe04a904468c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Nested interactions between chemosynthetic lucinid bivalves and seagrass promote ecosystem functioning in contaminated sediments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-227486","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Studies have indicated that underdiagnosis and diagnostic delay are common in celiac disease. Therefore, it is important to increase our knowledge of what symptoms and biomarkers could identify undiagnosed cases of celiac disease. Methods: We screened for celiac disease antibodies in stored blood samples from 16,776 participants in eight population-based studies examined during 1976–2012. Undiagnosed celiac seropositivity was defined as celiac disease antibody positivity (IgG-deamidated gliadin peptide above 10.0 U/mL and/or IgA-tissue transglutaminase (TTG) or IgG-TTG above 7.0 U/mL) without a known diagnosis of celiac disease in the National Patient Register. In all studies general health symptoms were recorded by participant-completed questionnaire, including self-perceived health, tiredness, headache and gastrointestinal symptoms. Furthermore, blood samples were drawn for analyses of biomarkers e.g. hemoglobin, blood glucose, cholesterol, liver parameters and vitamins. The participants with undiagnosed celiac seropositivity were matched by sex, age and study with four controls among the celiac disease antibody negative participants. Results: We excluded, five participants with known celiac disease, resulting in a population of 16,771 participants. In this population 1% (169/16,771) had undiagnosed celiac seropositivity. There were no statistically significant differences in symptoms between cases and controls. Undiagnosed celiac seropositivity was associated with low blood cholesterol (< 5 mmol/L) and low hemoglobin (< 7.3 mmol/L for women and < 8.3 mmol/L for men). Conclusion: In this general population study, undiagnosed cases of celiac seropositivity did not have more symptoms than controls, confirming the diagnostic difficulties of celiac disease and the low prognostic value of symptoms for a diagnosis of celiac disease. Furthermore, decreased levels of cholesterol and/or hemoglobin in the blood were associated with undiagnosed celiac seropositivity.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kårhus, Line Lund","Petersen, Janne","Leth-Møller, Katja Biering","Møllehave, Line Tang","Madsen, Anja Lykke","Thuesen, Betina Heinsbæk","Schwarz, Peter","Rumessen, Jüri J.","Linneberg, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416753"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Antibodies","Biomarkers","Celiac disease","Epidemiology","Screening","Symptoms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"symptoms and biomarkers associated with undiagnosed celiac seropositivity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-021-01667-y","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416753","identifier":[{"id":"33639838","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85101842413","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7913457","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-26f1af74-9dc6-4272-a3c1-1cafe1ed6516"],"keyword":["Antibodies","Biomarkers","Celiac disease","Epidemiology","Screening","Symptoms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F58412B081EB5AA7698705A6B39A2A95"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12876-021-01667-y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258492391/Symptoms_and_biomarkers_associated_with_undiagnosed_celiac_seropositivity.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Lund","key":"kårhuspau","last":"Kårhus","name":"Kårhus, Line Lund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Janne","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"1cb72724-54f8-4ca1-a201-bfa4a354a129","name":"Petersen, Janne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katja Biering","key":"lethmøllerpau","last":"Leth-Møller","name":"Leth-Møller, Katja Biering","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Line Tang","key":"møllehavepau","last":"Møllehave","locid":"3ab9da70-f231-4a76-9416-d00f3d12275a","name":"Møllehave, Line Tang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja Lykke","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Anja Lykke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Betina Heinsbæk","key":"thuesenpau","last":"Thuesen","name":"Thuesen, Betina Heinsbæk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter","key":"schwarzpau","last":"Schwarz","locid":"058b1228-5dc0-458a-a98c-3faded28305b","name":"Schwarz, Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jüri J.","key":"rumessenpau","last":"Rumessen","name":"Rumessen, Jüri J.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33639838"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12876-021-01667-y","issn":["1471230X"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Gastroenterology","paperid":"90","status":"p","title":"BMC Gastroenterology","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101842413"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-26f1af74-9dc6-4272-a3c1-1cafe1ed6516"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Symptoms and biomarkers associated with undiagnosed celiac seropositivity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-416753","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Diagnosed celiac disease (CD) is associated with lymphoproliferative malignancy and gastrointestinal cancer, but little is known about the long-term consequences of undiagnosed CD. We aimed to investigate long-term consequences of undiagnosed CD for mortality and incidence of cancer and other chronic diseases. METHODS: We screened biobank serum samples for immunoglobulin (Ig) A and IgG tissue transglutaminase (TTG) and IgG deamidated gliadin peptide in a study of 8 population-based cohort studies comprising 16,776 participants examined during 1976-2012 and followed with >99% complete follow-up in Danish nationwide registries until December 31, 2017, regarding vital status and incidence of diseases. Undiagnosed CD was defined as antibody positivity (IgA-TTG or IgG-TTG >= 7 U/mL and/or IgG deamidated gliadin peptide >= 10 U/mL) in individuals without a diagnosis of CD recorded in the National Patient Register. Hazard ratios (HRs) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) were estimated by Cox regression analyses with age as the underlying time scale. RESULTS: The prevalence of undiagnosed CD was 1.0% with no statistically significant increase over time. Undiagnosed CD was associated with increased risk of cancer overall (HR, 1.57; 95% CI, 1.16-2.11), gastrointestinal cancer (HR, 2.33; 95% CI, 1.35-4.04), cancer of the uterus (HR, 3.95; 95% CI, 1.46-10.69), breast cancer (HR, 1.98; 95% CI, 1.02-3.82), head and neck cancer (HR, 3.12; 95% CI, 1.15-8.43), and cardiovascular disease (HR, 1.37; 95% CI, 1.01-1.85). We found no statistically significant association between undiagnosed CD and mortality (HR, 1.19; 95% CI, 0.87-1.61). DISCUSSION: Undiagnosed CD was associated with increased risk of cardiovascular disease and cancer suggesting that untreated CD has serious long-term health consequences not only affecting the gastrointestinal tract (see Visual Abstract, Supplementary Digital Content,).","author_count":8,"contributors":["Karhus, Line Lund","Skaaby, Tea","Petersen, Janne","Madsen, Anja Lykke","Thuesen, Betina Heinsbaek","Schwarz, Peter","Rumessen, Juri J.","Linneberg, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-461088"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cancer","Disease","Gluten free diet","Individuals","Malignancy","Mortality","NATIONAL HEALTH","Population","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term consequences of undiagnosed celiac seropositivity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-461088","identifier":[{"id":"85092680283","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000576018400024","type":"wos"},{"id":"32558687","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-71408eac-d7ef-41b3-b70a-69a9a2a98cf4"],"keyword":["CANCER","DISEASE","GLUTEN-FREE DIET","INCREASING PREVALENCE","INDIVIDUALS","MALIGNANCY","MORTALITY","NATIONAL-HEALTH","POPULATION","RISK"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8747C60B92AC4DBBC6E2F9E16638304A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Line Lund","key":"karhuspau","last":"Karhus","name":"Karhus, Line Lund","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tea","key":"skaabypau","last":"Skaaby","name":"Skaaby, Tea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janne","ke